DTSTART:20260805T120000Z
DTEND:20260805T133000Z
SUMMARY:(CS)²AI Online™: Engineering Expertise-Core Skills for ICS/OT Cybersecurity
DESCRIPTION:Nashville Cyber Security for Control Systems Industrial control systems and operational technology sit at the center of the world's critical infrastructure — and the practitioners defending them need a fundamentally different skillset than traditional IT security teams. **[Join us for a (CS)²AI Online™ Seminar: Engineering Expertise-Core Skills for ICS/OT Cybersecurity](https://events.zoom.us/ev/AkelfcRk7xL1iGgzTbB7dc0p_zqI23zpZcYN-FLD1g2E8nsNXREt~Ak5X3Hzq7cOjaV1aW8e7x_mWDF96lkIYagLlXwyCpG8Sd8VcE4kADZIEM5UMB_mTTBWUIn0lcx7fNtkgghve3jM_Kw)\,** a panel discussion bringing together leading experts to break down what it actually takes to build and sustain a career in ICS/OT cybersecurity. Our speakers will cover the foundational and advanced competencies every OT security practitioner needs\, including: * Understanding industrial protocols\, PLCs\, SCADA\, and control system architecture * Bridging the IT/OT divide — translating security concepts across engineering and cybersecurity teams * Risk assessment and threat modeling specific to physical processes and safety systems * Incident response and recovery when uptime and safety are non-negotiable * Navigating standards and frameworks like IEC 62443\, NIST SP 800-82\, and sector-specific regulations * Career pathways: certifications\, hands-on experience\, and how to break into the field Whether you're an IT security professional looking to move into OT\, an engineer expanding into cybersecurity\, or a practitioner sharpening your existing skills\, this session will give you a clear-eyed view of what the field demands — and how to get there. **Who should attend:** Security analysts\, control systems engineers\, IT/OT convergence teams\, CISOs and security leaders overseeing industrial environments\, and anyone exploring a career in critical infrastructure protection. **[CLICK HERE TO REGISTER FOR THE EVENT](https://events.zoom.us/ev/AkelfcRk7xL1iGgzTbB7dc0p_zqI23zpZcYN-FLD1g2E8nsNXREt~Ak5X3Hzq7cOjaV1aW8e7x_mWDF96lkIYagLlXwyCpG8Sd8VcE4kADZIEM5UMB_mTTBWUIn0lcx7fNtkgghve3jM_Kw)** \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\- Becoming a paid member is quick and easy (and helps us keep offering free educational opportunities!). Please join now! [https://www.cs2ai.org/plans-pricing](https://www.cs2ai.org/plans-pricing) All past seminars and symposiums are available to paid [CS2AI.ORG](http://cs2ai.org/) members. Check out the Resources area of our website in the Members Portal [https://www.cs2ai.org/](https://www.cs2ai.org/) Certificates for Professional Development/Continuing Education Units (PDUs/CEUs) are available for all registered individuals who attend at least one hour of the event. [https://www.cs2ai.org/get-involved](https://www.cs2ai.org/get-involved) \\*Please note that (CS)²AI Online™ events are provided free of charge as educational career development content through the support of our paid members and the generous contributions of our corporate Strategic Alliance Partners. Contact information used in registering for our directly supported seminars may be shared with sponsors funding those specific events. Unless noted on our Zoom Event registration page\, all events are open for direct funding support. © Control System Cyber Security Association International 2026 | Source: Nashville Cyber Security for Control Systems | Tags: ciso\, cyber\, cybersecurity\, risk\, security | https://www.meetup.com/nashville-cyber-security-for-control-systems/events/315901139/
LOCATION:
URL:https://www.meetup.com/nashville-cyber-security-for-control-systems/events/315901139/
END:VEVENT
