SUMMARY:Woodworking Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Noisebridge Hackerspace -please read the whole updated description!- Come to work on your own projects and get some feedback from your fellow woodchucks. We have a planer\, drill presses\, hand tools\, a table saw\, and much more! ###################### **starting June 8 we will be taking a break from the intensive power tool trainings provided in previous sessions.** For the next few weeks we want to use wood night as a time for actively working on projects and designing ideas for your projects. Happy to help with some guided use of the tools\, but for now no full training will be offered. If you are new to the woodshop you are still welcome to join\, just know that we will not provide a full training on the tools. If you have significant experience using a Tablesaw\, mitre saw\, planer etc then this should not be an issue. We do have some scrap wood available\, but bringing some wood for your project\, especially if it is larger or more crafty\, is highly encouraged. We recommend getting your wood at Lowe’s (cheaper) Discount builders supply (closer to NB) or Beronio (higher quality and carry lots of hardwoods). Please feel free to ask questions on the discord if you are unsure about what to get for your project. | Source: DC415 San Francisco | Tags: security | https://www.meetup.com/noisebridge/events/315783486/
LOCATION:
URL:https://www.meetup.com/noisebridge/events/315783486/
END:VEVENT
